cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Lessons in AI from an Image Classifier"
abstract: >-
  An eight-lesson curriculum and a Streamlit lab that walk through how an
  image classifier learns, from pixels and loss to evaluation and the
  hardware that runs the arithmetic. Each lesson states its objectives,
  explains the idea, and ends with exercises. Upload two or more labeled
  image sets, or use the built-in shapes, and train a ResNet-18 from
  ImageNet weights or from scratch.
version: 1.1.1
